tegies to optimize RTS outcomes in female athletes. Keywords: ACL; anterior cruciate ligament; ACLR; return to sport; female; sex Anterior cruciate ligament (ACL) injuries represent one of with significant implications for athletic careers and long- the most common and significant knee injuries in sport, term knee health. The incidence of ACL injury has risen over the last decades, particularly in the younger popula- tion and athletes, with pediatric ACL reconstructions *Address correspondence to Darby Amelia Elliott, Department of (ACLRs) increasing by .40% in Norway between 2005 Surgery and 
